men under any  circumstances often hinders him from  helping and protecting those around him  this can for example be seen in his  fight against Khalifa from cp9 during  the Ennis Lobby arc and the conflict  between his loyalty towards eff and his  loyalty towards his crew and up in the  whole cake island arc which purpose has  been deeply misunderstood exactly for  the same reason people thought that the  arc was all about Sanji  stronger and catching up to Luffy and  Zorro and there was a lot of  disappointment when that didn't happen  but as we just saw that's not what this  character is actually about whole cake  island was Sanji's arc because his  ideals that he strives to keep up  finally pushed him into a moral corner  where he had no choice but to change he  had to experience the problems and pain  that sticking to his ideals could mean  and he had to learn and accept to trust  his captain and his crew in order to be  able to keep them alive in the future in  other words  Sanji had to grow as a character to stay  loyal to his values so the next time you  read the whole cake island arc I ask you  to keep that in mind and try to look at  the events from that perspective you  will see that the entire arc gets an  entirely new gravity for Sanji's  character when you stop looking at him  the same way you would look at Zorro a  Luffy Sanji is a fascinating character  because his personality and his combat  skills make his character seem  inconsistent and contradictive at times  but it's important to realize how great  it is for destroy at KU to have someone  as kind and compassionate as Sanji on  the crew that also has the power to act  upon it so despite being close to luffy  and Zorro in terms of combat ability his  character arc is very different and  unique inside the crew being a true  gentleman brings many challenges and  hardships with it but it also makes  Sanji so incredibly important for the  true and the entire story plus he can  cook what else could anyone ask for hey  everybody thank you so much for watching  I feel like there often is a lot of  competition between Sanji and Zorro fans  but I personally think that there's no  issue in loving both characters for  different reasons yes both can fight but  apart from that both of them have  amazingly complex and interesting  personalities and ideals and I think  that both will be equally important to  help Luffy and the crew reach their  goals in the future what are your  thoughts on his character though and  what other defining moments can you  think of let me know your thoughts in  the comments below  starting this week you can also support  me and my work on patreon if you're  interested in helping me make more  embedded videos you can find a link to  my page in the description below you  will get free access to all of my  artwork and early access to my major  videos if you like this video don't  forget to like share and subscribe to be  notified for any future  kontin of mine or dislike don't share  and unsubscribe it's a free world people  I hope to see Iran next time and until  then have a great week  oh yeah and don't forget to turn your  notifications on because YouTube can  sometimes be forgetful bye  you  [Music]
 

